## Why This Is Asked
Real-world WAL tail latency can throttle throughput in bursts; this question probes capability to diagnose IO path bottlenecks and apply production-grade mitigations that don’t compromise data integrity.

## Key Concepts
- IO scheduling and blk-mq
- Per-disk and per-tenant I/O control (cgroups v2)
- CPU/IRQ affinity and NUMA awareness
- WAL isolation strategies and PostgreSQL tuning
- Rigorous load-testing and safe rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js: simple iostat collector for WAL latency analysis
const {spawn} = require('child_process');
const log = require('fs').createWriteStream('/var/log/iostat_wal.log', {flags:'a'});
const proc = spawn('iostat', ['-x','1']);
proc.stdout.on('data', data => log.write(data));
proc.stderr.on('data', d => process.stderr.write(d));
```

